\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. See, amid the winter's snow,
\par Born for us on earth below,
\par See, the Lamb of God appears,
\par Promised from eternal years.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem:
\par Christ is born in Bethlehem!\i0 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Lo, within a manger lies
\par He who built the starry skies,
\par He who, throned in height sublime,
\par Sits amid the cherubim.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem:
\par Christ is born in Bethlehem!\i0 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Say, ye holy shepherds, say,
\par What your joyful news to-day;
\par Wherefore have ye left your sheep
\par On the lonely mountain steep?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem:
\par Christ is born in Bethlehem!\i0 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. As we watched at dead of night,
\par Lo, we saw a wondrous light:
\par Angels, singing peace on earth,
\par Told us of the Saviour's birth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem:
\par Christ is born in Bethlehem!\i0 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Sacred Infant, all divine,
\par What a tender love was Thine,
\par Thus to come from highest bliss
\par Down to such a world as this!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem:
\par Christ is born in Bethlehem!\i0 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Teach, O teach us, holy Child,
\par By Thy face to meek and mild,
\par Teach us to resemble Thee
\par In Thy sweet humility.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem:
\par Christ is born in Bethlehem!\i0\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

